{
  "A": "Research asymptotic algorithm improvements in src/est_matriz_seq.c. Replace bubble sorting with a stable O(rows log rows) double sort, considering an insertion-sort cutoff for short columns. Replace quadratic mode counting with a linear scan of sorted equal-value runs: retain the earliest maximum-frequency run and return -1 when nothing repeats. Measure sorting and mode changes separately, then together. Use initialized state rather than reproducing the source's uninitialized reads; preserve its float narrowing of the selected mode for reference compatibility. Preserve equal-value stability, including signed zeros, and provide a semantics-preserving fallback when unordered comparisons invalidate sorting/run-counting assumptions. Do not restrict samples to integers, positive numbers, or observed values. Leave accumulation order and I/O unchanged to isolate these improvements.",
  "B": "Research column-level execution and numerical dataflow. Columns are independent and already contiguous: fuse arithmetic and harmonic mean passes while preserving each accumulator's original row order, then retain sorted-order variance accumulation. Evaluate processing complete columns in one coarse-grained parallel region with up to four workers, only if supported by the unchanged build. Keep sorting scratch private and output serial. Compare serial execution against parallel variants; use a general workload-based threshold because thread startup can overwhelm a roughly 9 ms run. If threading is unavailable, prioritize serial fusion and scratch reuse rather than changing the compiler. Avoid within-column parallel reductions, reassociation, approximate reciprocals, and one-pass variance formulas. Keep sort/mode implementations replaceable so G can integrate A's work.",
  "C": "Research input/output overhead independently of the statistical algorithms. First evaluate buffering improvements around existing formatted I/O; then consider a bounded buffered reader using a correctly rounded general conversion such as strtod. Preserve the accepted double syntax, signs, exponents, whitespace handling, tokens spanning buffers, and valid EOF behavior; do not substitute an integer-only or limited-decimal parser. Keep the current column-major storage unless measurements justify additional layout work. Evaluate buffered output using the same one-decimal formatting, metric order, trailing spaces, and newlines. Bound additional memory and avoid unnecessary whole-input copies. Leave arithmetic and sorting unchanged so any gain or regression can be attributed to I/O.",
  "G": "Integrate measured programs from A/B/C, not presumed additive improvements. Obtain each candidate's source changes, unchanged-harness correctness result, timings, and semantic caveats. Start from the fastest validated standalone candidate, add isolated compatible changes, and measure combinations within the existing budget and measurement protocol. Reassess parallel thresholds after algorithmic acceleration: faster sorting can make threading counterproductive, while parsing may become dominant. Preserve original-order mean/harmonic accumulation, sorted-order variance, median arithmetic, sample-variance denominator, mode conversion behavior, and exact seven-line formatting. Do not silently repair zero, singleton, nonfinite, or rounding-sensitive behavior. Escalate unexplained mode/oracle conflicts rather than exploiting allocator state. Retain the best validated standalone or partial integration whenever the full combination is slower. Change no tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions.",
  "analysis": "Only Problem B matches the supplied source. For R rows and C columns, both bubble sorting and nested mode counting cost O(CR²); other numerical passes cost O(CR). Replacing both quadratic stages is the strongest source-based opportunity, while the existing column-major layout supports independent column processing. The baseline passed four correctness cases and averaged 9.264 ms, with samples spanning approximately 9.169–9.447 ms. There is no hotspot profile or input-size breakdown, so sorting dominance, I/O dominance, and parallel gains remain hypotheses; startup overhead and measurement variation may matter. The target is four-core ARM64 without GPUs. Compatibility requires care: means precede sorting, variance follows sorting, and mode reads uninitialized counters and stores its winner in float. Passing four cases does not establish correctness for every valid input. All research should preserve deterministic reference behavior where defined, avoid exploiting undefined behavior, and report specification/reference conflicts explicitly."
}